steps.description:
ArgoCD uses DexIDP and it supports [authenticating proxy](https://dexidp.io/docs/connectors/authproxy/). I use it with [Vouch](https://github.com/vouch/vouch-proxy), Okta and Nginx. Basically, ArgoCD is gated by nginx that does setup user roles based on Vouch HTTP headers. e.g. 
```
    map
```yaml
map $http_x_vouch_user $__argocd_role {
      default Engineers;
      admin@example.com Administrators;
    }

    server {
      listen 80 default_server;
      server_name _;

      location / {
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;

        proxy_set_header X-Remote-User $http_x_vouch_user;
        proxy_set_header X-Remote-Group $__argocd_role;
        proxy_set_header Host $FQDN;
        proxy_set_header Authorization "";

        proxy_pass http://argocd-server.argocd.svc.cluster.local./;
      }
    }
```

